      "content": "Feeling dismissed by a distracted doctor is understandably frustrating, especially when you are trying to manage a condition that requires such precise dietary balance. However, relying on \"small amounts\" or \"surprisingly,\" can be risky because the interaction between Vitamin K and warfarin is cumulative; even consistent, moderate daily increases in greens can silently alter your blood thinning effects over time. It is crucial for your safety to find a time to speak with your doctor or bring a written log of your protein packs to help them understand your dietary goals and adjust your medication instead. Your heart is precious, and being proactive about your health is the right step, but doing so safely requires a plan that keeps your INR within a safe range.",
